{
    public const TEMPLATES = [
        'en' => [
            'Ashwini' => 'Born under Ashwini, ruled by the twin Ashwini Kumaras (divine healers) and symbolized by the horse, you tend to be quick, energetic, and eager to be first — a pioneering Deva-Gana nature that moves fast and heals fast, in body and in spirit alike. This often favors work in medicine, emergency response, travel, or any field rewarding speed and initiative; a restless streak means routine, slow-moving careers rarely hold your interest for long. In family life you bring warmth and a protective instinct, though your independence can make settling down feel like it happens later and on your own terms.',
            'Bharani' => 'Born under Bharani, ruled by Yama (lord of transformation and restraint) and symbolized by the elephant, you carry a Manushya-Gana intensity — strong willpower, deep passions, and a capacity to endure hardship that others would find crushing. This often favors careers demanding discipline and transformation of raw material into something refined: law, agriculture, the arts, or any work that tests endurance before it rewards it. In family life your loyalty runs deep once committed, though a tendency to carry burdens silently is worth watching, especially around close relationships.',
            'Krittika' => 'Born under Krittika, ruled by Agni (the fire god) and symbolized by a blade or flame, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana sharpness — a cutting intellect, high standards, and a readiness to burn away what no longer serves you. This often favors leadership, critique, cooking, or any field where precision and purifying judgment are assets; patience with mediocrity is rarely your strong suit. In family life you are fiercely protective of those you consider yours, though a sharp tongue under stress is worth tempering.',
            'Rohini' => 'Born under Rohini, ruled by Brahma (the creator) and symbolized by the serpent, you carry a Manushya-Gana magnetism — charm, creativity, and a deep love of beauty, comfort, and growth that makes you naturally persuasive. This often favors the arts, agriculture, luxury goods, or any field rewarding patient cultivation and an eye for quality; you build value slowly and durably. In family life you are affectionate and nurturing, though possessiveness toward people and possessions alike is a trait worth managing with care.',
            'Mrigashira' => 'Born under Mrigashira, ruled by Soma (the Moon god) and symbolized by the deer\'s head, you carry a Deva-Gana curiosity — gentle, searching, and perpetually drawn toward the next discovery, whether in ideas, places, or people. This often favors research, writing, travel, or any field that rewards exploration over repetition; a wandering attention means you do best with variety built into the work itself. In family life you bring warmth and gentleness, though a restless need to keep searching can make commitment feel like it arrives gradually rather than all at once.',
            'Ardra' => 'Born under Ardra, ruled by Rudra (the storm god) and symbolized by a teardrop, you carry a Manushya-Gana intensity forged through difficulty — sharp intelligence and real emotional depth that often develops precisely because life has asked something hard of you. This often favors research, technology, psychology, or crisis-adjacent work where the ability to stay clear-headed in storms is a genuine asset. In family life your feelings run deep and can be turbulent before they settle; close relationships benefit when you let that intensity be seen rather than held back.',
            'Punarvasu' => 'Born under Punarvasu, ruled by Aditi (mother of the gods) and symbolized by a quiver of arrows, you carry a Deva-Gana resilience — an ability to return and renew after setbacks that genuinely sets you apart, paired with generosity and philosophical calm. This often favors teaching, counseling, writing, or any field rewarding patience and the capacity to start again without bitterness. In family life you are nurturing and forgiving, often the one who repairs a rift others have given up on, though your own needs can go quietly unspoken in the process.',
            'Pushya' => 'Born under Pushya, ruled by Brihaspati (Jupiter, guru of the gods) and widely considered one of the most auspicious nakshatras, you carry a Deva-Gana steadiness — nurturing, responsible, and genuinely wise beyond what your years alone would suggest. This often favors teaching, counseling, administration, or spiritual work, where being trusted with others\' wellbeing comes naturally. In family life you are the dependable one, often a caretaker for parents and siblings alike, though you benefit from occasionally letting others look after you in return.',
            'Ashlesha' => 'Born under Ashlesha, ruled by the Nagas (serpent deities) and symbolized by a coiled snake, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana perceptiveness — intuitive, strategic, and able to read undercurrents others miss entirely. This often favors psychology, research, healing professions, or any field rewarding sharp insight into what\'s really going on beneath the surface. In family life your attachments run deep and can be protective to the point of possessiveness; trust, once broken, is hard-won back, so honesty from the start matters more than usual.',
            'Magha' => 'Born under Magha, ruled by the Pitris (ancestral spirits) and symbolized by a royal throne, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana regality — a natural sense of dignity, tradition, and leadership, often with a strong pull toward honoring family lineage and heritage. This often favors administration, politics, heritage-related work, or any field where authority and respect for tradition are assets. In family life you take ancestry and family name seriously, often becoming a natural head of the household, though pride is worth tempering when it edges into stubbornness.',
            'Purva Phalguni' => 'Born under Purva Phalguni, ruled by Bhaga (god of fortune and marital bliss) and symbolized by the front legs of a bed, you carry a Manushya-Gana warmth — romantic, pleasure-loving, and genuinely gifted at making life comfortable and enjoyable for yourself and others. This often favors the arts, entertainment, hospitality, or any field rewarding charm and creativity. In family life and relationships you are affectionate and loyal, with marriage and partnership often central themes, though a taste for comfort is worth balancing with discipline.',
            'Uttara Phalguni' => 'Born under Uttara Phalguni, ruled by Aryaman (god of patronage and contracts) and symbolized by the back legs of a bed, you carry a Manushya-Gana reliability — generous, principled, and genuinely good at forming lasting partnerships, whether in marriage, friendship, or business. This often favors counseling, contract-based work, helping professions, or any field built on trust between people. In family life you are a steady, generous presence, often the one others lean on in a crisis, though it\'s worth remembering to ask for help in return.',
            'Hasta' => 'Born under Hasta, ruled by Savitar (the sun god of skill) and symbolized by a hand, you carry a Deva-Gana dexterity — skillful, witty, and genuinely good with your hands and your words alike, able to shape raw material (or a conversation) into something useful. This often favors craftsmanship, medicine, comedy, or any field rewarding fine motor skill and quick wit. In family life you are helpful and resourceful, often the one who fixes what\'s broken, though a restless need to stay busy is worth balancing with rest.',
            'Chitra' => 'Born under Chitra, ruled by Tvashtar (the celestial architect) and symbolized by a bright jewel, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana flair — a strong aesthetic sense, creativity, and a genuine love of designing and building things that are both functional and beautiful. This often favors architecture, design, engineering, or any field rewarding a sharp eye for form. In family life you bring color and charisma, often standing out even within your own household, though vanity is worth watching when the pursuit of appearance outpaces substance.',
            'Swati' => 'Born under Swati, ruled by Vayu (the wind god) and symbolized by a young sprout bending in the breeze, you carry a Deva-Gana independence — adaptable, diplomatic, and genuinely uncomfortable being pinned down or controlled by anyone. This often favors trade, diplomacy, law, or any field rewarding flexibility and fair dealing. In family life you value your freedom even within close relationships, which works best with a partner who doesn\'t mistake that independence for a lack of commitment.',
            'Vishakha' => 'Born under Vishakha, ruled by Indra and Agni jointly and symbolized by a decorated archway, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana determination — goal-driven, ambitious, and genuinely willing to pursue two things at once (worldly success and inner purpose) without choosing between them. This often favors competitive fields, politics, business leadership, or any work rewarding sustained drive toward a clear target. In family life your focus on goals can mean relationships take a back seat during ambitious periods; a conscious effort to stay present pays off here.',
            'Anuradha' => 'Born under Anuradha, ruled by Mitra (god of friendship and alliance) and symbolized by a lotus, you carry a Deva-Gana devotion — loyal, disciplined, and genuinely gifted at building lasting friendships and alliances across cultures and distances. This often favors diplomacy, international work, organizing, or any field rewarding the ability to unite people toward a shared goal. In family life you are devoted and dependable, often maintaining close bonds across long distances, though old wounds from betrayal (if any) are worth consciously healing rather than carrying forward.',
            'Jyeshtha' => 'Born under Jyeshtha, ruled by Indra (king of the gods) and symbolized by a circular amulet or umbrella, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana authority — protective, responsible, and genuinely comfortable being the one in charge, often shouldering more responsibility than your position formally requires. This often favors management, protective professions, or any field where being depended upon is the point. In family life you take the role of eldest or protector seriously, sometimes at real cost to yourself; learning to delegate is a recurring, worthwhile lesson.',
            'Mula' => 'Born under Mula, ruled by Nirriti (goddess of destruction and dissolution) and symbolized by a bundle of roots, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana thoroughness — a drive to get to the root of things, investigate deeply, and dismantle what\'s false before rebuilding on firmer ground. This often favors research, philosophy, medicine, or any field rewarding the willingness to dig past comfortable surface answers. In family life your path can include real upheaval before stability settles in; that disruption, while unsettling, is often the mechanism through which lasting foundations actually get built.',
            'Purva Ashadha' => 'Born under Purva Ashadha, ruled by Apas (the water deity) and symbolized by an elephant tusk or fan, you carry a Manushya-Gana conviction — proud, persuasive, and genuinely hard to defeat once you\'ve committed to a position, with real skill at winning others over through argument and charisma. This often favors law, public speaking, sales, or any field rewarding the ability to make a compelling case. In family life your pride and independence are strengths, though learning to concede small points gracefully smooths relationships considerably.',
            'Uttara Ashadha' => 'Born under Uttara Ashadha, ruled by the Vishvadevas (universal gods) and symbolized by an elephant tusk, you carry a Manushya-Gana integrity — principled, patient, and genuinely committed to seeing long efforts through to a lasting, respected conclusion rather than a quick win. This often favors leadership, law, long-term institutional work, or any field rewarding staying power. In family life you build slowly but durably, earning deep respect over time, though success and recognition often arrive later in life than your early efforts might suggest.',
            'Shravana' => 'Born under Shravana, ruled by Vishnu (the preserver) and symbolized by an ear, you carry a Deva-Gana attentiveness — a genuine gift for listening, learning, and gathering and transmitting knowledge faithfully. This often favors teaching, writing, broadcasting, counseling, or any field built on careful listening and clear communication. In family life you are a connector, often the one who keeps extended family and old friendships in touch across years and distances, with a naturally good memory for people\'s stories.',
            'Dhanishta' => 'Born under Dhanishta, ruled by the eight Vasus (gods of material abundance) and symbolized by a drum, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana rhythm — energetic, musical, and genuinely driven toward wealth, recognition, and group achievement, often with real talent in music or rhythm-based pursuits. This often favors music, real estate, finance, team leadership, or any field rewarding ambition paired with charisma. In family life you value status and material comfort for your household, though generosity sits alongside that ambition more often than stereotype suggests.',
            'Shatabhisha' => 'Born under Shatabhisha, ruled by Varuna (god of cosmic law and the healing waters) and symbolized by an empty circle, you carry a Rakshasa-Gana independence — a natural healer and truth-seeker with a strong pull toward solitude, research, and unconventional or alternative approaches. This often favors medicine, science, astrology, technology, or any field rewarding independent, skeptical inquiry. In family life you value your own space more than most and can seem reserved or secretive, though those let fully in experience real loyalty and care.',
            'Purva Bhadrapada' => 'Born under Purva Bhadrapada, ruled by Aja Ekapada (a fierce, one-footed form of the fire deity) and symbolized by a two-faced man or funeral cot, you carry a Manushya-Gana intensity — passionate, idealistic, and drawn to extremes, often with a spiritual or transformative streak that sits uneasily alongside worldly ambition. This often favors spiritual teaching, research into the unknown, finance, or any field where intensity of focus is an asset rather than a liability. In family life your passions run deep, and learning to moderate between idealism and practicality smooths what can otherwise be a turbulent path.',
            'Uttara Bhadrapada' => 'Born under Uttara Bhadrapada, ruled by Ahir Budhnya (serpent of the deep) and symbolized by a pair of back legs of a funeral cot or a serpent in water, you carry a Manushya-Gana depth — calm on the surface with considerable wisdom and emotional resilience underneath, often gained through genuinely difficult experience. This often favors counseling, spiritual work, insurance, charitable work, or any field rewarding quiet strength and patience with others\' suffering. In family life you are a stabilizing, protective presence, particularly valuable during a crisis, though your own depths are worth sharing rather than carrying entirely alone.',
            'Revati' => 'Born under Revati, ruled by Pushan (the nourisher and guide of travelers) and symbolized by a fish, you carry a Deva-Gana gentleness — compassionate, nurturing, and genuinely drawn to guiding and protecting others, especially those more vulnerable than yourself. This often favors caregiving professions, hospitality, travel and transport, or any field centered on looking after others\' wellbeing. In family life you are soft-hearted and self-sacrificing, often putting others\' needs well ahead of your own; this nakshatra, closing the full nakshatra cycle, also carries a classical theme of completion and gentle closure in life\'s major chapters.',
        ],
        'hi' => [],
        'gu' => [],
    ];
}
